  "shared_mechanics": [
    "Static MaximumHandSize(u16) and existing NoMaximumHandSize share an independent sparse owned HandSizeState clock, exact source-incarnation rows, and latest lasting infinity setter per player. Current controller and shared continuous ability availability determine which source applies; suppression/control change does not retimestamp, while departure forgets the exact row.",
    "The existing private lasting-grant presence marker is retained for compatibility and checked against the cold lasting timestamp. It never overrides a later finite setter: maximum_hand_size chooses the newest applicable finite or infinite setting, with default seven.",
    "Before any finite setter participates, infinity-only chronology is semantically redundant to the existing effective public bool. Once finite rules actually commit, an optional public hand_size_timeline honestly exposes every retained source/lasting row and both current maxima. This condition is ordinary observer behavior, independent of recorder/schema projection; it is never field stripping.",
    "Existing ability_source_timestamps and RoleState clock remain unchanged for hand-only events. Mixed finite entry batches use owned APNAP/controller timestamp choices before whole commit. Physical entry order and chosen timestamp order produce the same canonical new source-vector representation. Pure infinity batches add no old-game choices; shared existing source choices retain their relative order.",
    "Actual and projected entries use independently owned hand chronology, with hand-only entries filtered out of role timestamp registration. Virtual departures forget exact source rows and retain lasting grants; parent state is unchanged. No new mana funding loop or unrelated power/cost predicate is introduced.",
    "One above_hand_limit query serves ordinary/repeated cleanup entry, selected-discard completion, and end-turn continuation. Discards precede end-of-turn effect expiration and remain the existing private simultaneous discard transaction.",
    "ControllerHandDeficit(u16) captures saturating current hand difference once for the packet controller. The existing AtStep hand threshold checks both when triggering and resolving; DrawScaled feeds the existing interruptible individual-draw/ordinal/empty-library pipeline. Source movement/control/suppression never redirects the packet."
  ],
